{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Merges button presses that reach the app twice into one press per click."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["iOS","iPadOS","Mac Catalyst"],"tokens":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ButtonMerger","kind":"identifier"}]}]},{"mentions":["doc:\/\/com.nth.headwire\/documentation\/Headwire\/FeaturesAndInput"],"kind":"mentions"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A physical trackpad or mouse click arrives both from GCMouse and as a UIKit pointer touch."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Tap-to-click is synthesized by iPadOS and arrives only as the pointer touch. A button counts"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"as down while any source holds it, so the Mac gets one down on the first source and one up"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"when the last lets go."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The two reports of one click need not overlap. On an iPad Pro 11-inch (2nd generation, iPadOS"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"27.2) a short click often arrived as the whole of one source’s press and release, then the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"other’s 1 to 4 ms later. A press from the other source within "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.nth.headwire\/documentation\/Headwire\/ButtonMerger\/echoWindow","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" of the release is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that echo, and it and its release are dropped."}]}]}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Input","identifiers":["doc:\/\/com.nth.headwire\/documentation\/Headwire\/InputSurface","doc:\/\/com.nth.headwire\/documentation\/Headwire\/InputSurface